    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01BZHwSgnGAC4LTh4wgvYJsE?thread=cmsg_01BZHwSgnGAC4LTh4wgvYJsESgfFwDt41Q2LvPimo5EdKU)_\n\nBefore: plugging the iPod into the Mac let Finder sync it straight away, which read and deleted `iPod_Control/iTunes/Play Counts`, so Legacy Scrobbler had nothing left to scrobble.\n\nAfter: `~/.config/listening/ipod-no-autosync` turns that off and can undo it.\n- `on` (default, safe to rerun) sets `dontAutomaticallySyncIPods = true` in `com.apple.AMPDevicesAgent` (Finder's device sync helper, 10.15+) and `com.apple.iTunes` (10.14 and earlier), then restarts `AMPDevicesAgent`. Earlier values are saved for `off`.\n- `status` shows both settings, the agent, mounted iPods and whether `Play Counts` is still on them.\n- `off` restores the values from before `on`.\n- `backup` copies `Play Counts` + `iTunesDB` from every mounted iPod to `$XDG_DATA_HOME/listening/ipod-backups/`, skipping unchanged copies.\n- `agent install|remove` adds a launchd agent (`StartOnMount`) that runs `backup` whenever a volume mounts.\n\nThe per-device Finder checkbox \"Automatically sync when this iPod is connected\" is not changed by the script; the docs and `on` output say to untick it once.\n\nHow: bash 3.2–compatible script in `.config/listening/`, a new section in `PLAN.org`, and a CHANGELOG entry. Stacked on #171 because `PLAN.org` only exists there.\n\nTesting: run in a Linux container against stand-ins for `uname`, `defaults`, `pgrep`, `killall` and `/Volumes` (`IPOD_VOLUMES` override): on → on again (no-op) → backup ×2 (second skipped) → off restored the original `false` and removed the unset key. **Not run on a Mac**: whether current macOS still honours the `AMPDevicesAgent` key, whether Finder reads Play Counts on connect even without syncing (the backup agent is the fallback and may lose that race), and the launchd agent.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCoTQdiqAtvt2N3KVo)_",
